@q 3:4-5

**"Bullock capitalists"** (Lloyd and Susanne Rudolph) are **middle peasants** who own some land and bullocks but are not rich; they became a strong political force in North India.

@section 3.2 | Land Reforms and Holdings

@q 3:6-8

@src1 3:1
@one U.P.P.C.S. (Mains) 2017
Which measures have been taken to make the agrarian structure conducive to agricultural growth?
@ans Abolition of Intermediaries, tenancy reforms and ceiling on land holdings
@end

@table
Land reform measure | Purpose
**Abolition of zamindari** (intermediaries) | First and most successful step (UP Zamindari Abolition Act, 1950)
**Tenancy reforms** | **Regulation of rent, security of tenure, ownership for tenants**
**Ceiling on landholdings** | Redistribute surplus land to the landless
**Consolidation of holdings** (chakbandi) | Join scattered plots; UP and Punjab led
Bhoodan (Vinoba Bhave, 1951) | Voluntary land gifts
@end

@table
Farm size class (Agriculture Census) | Area | Share of holdings (2015-16)
**Marginal** | Below 1 hectare | About **68%**
**Small** | **1-2 hectares** | About 18%
Semi-medium | 2-4 ha | About 9.5%
Medium | 4-10 ha | About 4%
Large | Above 10 ha | About 0.6%
Average holding | **1.08 ha** (falling every census) | -
@end

